🔢 Count Occurrences

Once we know the first and last positions:

Count = last - first + 1

For:

first = 1
last = 3
count = 3 - 1 + 1
      = 3

So 2 appears 3 times.

Time Complexity

Both searches use Binary Search:

Time:  O(log n)
Space: O(1)

Finding both first and last occurrence is still:

O(log n)
Key Takeaways
First occurrence → when found, continue left.
Last occurrence → when found, continue right.
Store the answer before continuing.
Works on a sorted array.
Time complexity: O(log n).
Space complexity: O(1).
